    verification pullOversightRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "723c08d3-e447-4639-8b4e-05cee2e19883"; :>> title = "Sprint 432 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-23"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049). AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN under rcRecurrence: the conscription class - designing the supervisor INTO the machinery - now has a named kill rule (D0204) and a memory; the recurrence risk is any future control whose enforcement path runs through human attention, and the review checklist question is now 'who pays the attention cost of this control?'. WELL: the reversal cost one sprint because the records and the asks were cleanly separated all along - removing push left pull intact with zero data loss. Estimate 2 pts, delivered 2."; }
